course: dictionary
lesson: 6348
title: Movable: able to move, or a date that changes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Movable means able to be moved from one place to another. It is not fixed. «Sea urchins are covered with movable spines that point towards a threat.» The spines can move, so they are not stuck in one position.
explain: Movable can also describe a holiday or festival that falls on a different date each year. «Easter is a movable feast» means its date changes from year to year. Christmas, on the other hand, always falls on 25 December.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Johannes Gutenberg began printing books with movable metal letters around 1450.» Could the letters be moved into different orders? Yes, so movable fits, and printers could arrange the words in many ways.
fact: Movable means able to be moved from one place to another; not fixed.
fact: «Movable type» means letters that can be picked up and put in different orders to print a page.
fact: Johannes Gutenberg began printing books with movable metal letters around 1450.
fact: Bi Sheng made clay movable type around 1040 AD, long before Gutenberg.
fact: A «movable feast» is a holiday or festival whose date changes each year, like Easter.
exercise: «The guzheng has strings over movable bridges.» What does movable mean here? | Always in the same place | Very heavy | Painted in bright colours | *Able to be moved, not fixed
exercise: «Easter is a movable feast.» What does movable mean here? | *Falling on a different date each year | Happening on the same date every year | Held in a shop | Shaped like a ball
exercise: Which of these is a movable part, one that can bend or turn? | A stone wall | A tree trunk | *A hinge on a door | A brick chimney
test: «Gutenberg's movable metal letters let printers put words in different orders.» Why were the letters called movable? | They could float on water | They were always fixed to the page | They were made of wood | *They could be moved and rearranged
test: Which of these is described as a movable feast? | Christmas Day | Bonfire Night | Boxing Day | *Easter
exam: «The table has a movable top, so it can be taken off.» What does movable mean? | *Able to be moved, not fixed | Made of glass | Painted red | Very tall
